        "original_id": "2a7dbbd0-7f2c-55e2-a572-58e6d0d10887",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Little Mermaid, The Strongest Man in the World, Aladdin, Pocahontas, Dinosaur, Home on the Range, The Prince and the Pauper\n- Companies: Walt Disney Feature Animation, Walt Disney Pictures\n- People: H. Lee Peterson, Kurt Russell\n- Places: Medfield College\n\nFacts:\n- The Strongest Man in the World is a 1975 Disney film starring Kurt Russell as a student at the fictional Medfield College.\n- The Little Mermaid is a 1989 American animated musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was an assistant editor for The Little Mermaid for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Aladdin, Pocahontas, Dinosaur, and Home on the Range for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for the short film The Prince and the Pauper, which stars Mickey Mouse, for Walt Disney Pictures.",
